(
  'The Art of the Pivot: When to Rebrand',
  'the-art-of-the-pivot-when-to-rebrand',
  '<p>In the ever-evolving landscape of business, staying relevant is key. A rebrand isn''t just about a new logo or a fresh coat of paint; it''s a strategic move to realign your business with its core values and market demands.</p><h2>Why Rebrand?</h2><p>Companies evolve. Your mission today might be different from what it was five years ago. If your visual identity and messaging no longer reflect who you are, it''s time for a change.</p><ul><li><strong>Market Shifts:</strong> Changes in consumer behavior or industry trends.</li><li><strong>New Audience:</strong> Targeting a different demographic.</li><li><strong>Mergers & Acquisitions:</strong> Combining cultures and identities.</li></ul><p>At CoreCraft, we help businesses navigate these complex transitions, ensuring that every element of the new brand tells a cohesive and compelling story.</p>',
  'A rebrand isn''t just about a new logo; it''s a strategic move to realign your business with its core values and market demands. Learn when and why to pivot.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542744173-8e7e53415bb0?q=80&w=2070&auto=format&fit=crop',
  true,
  'Sarah Jenkins'
),
(
  '5 Key Elements of a High-Converting Landing Page',
  '5-key-elements-of-a-high-converting-landing-page',
  '<p>You have seconds to capture a visitor''s attention. A high-converting landing page is a blend of art and science, designed to guide users toward a specific action.</p><h2>1. A Compelling Headline</h2><p>Your headline should clearly state the value proposition. What''s in it for the user?</p><h2>2. Clear Call-to-Action (CTA)</h2><p>Don''t make users guess what to do next. Use contrasting colors and action-oriented text.</p><h2>3. Social Proof</h2><p>Testimonials, case studies, and logos of trusted partners build credibility instantly.</p><p>Optimizing these elements can significantly lower your bounce rate and increase conversions. It''s about creating a seamless user journey from click to conversion.</p>',
  'You have seconds to capture a visitor''s attention. Discover the 5 essential elements that transform casual visitors into loyal customers.',
  'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1460925895917-afdab827c52f?q=80&w=2015&auto=format&fit=crop',
  true,
  'David Chen'
),
(
  'Why Storytelling is the Future of Marketing',
  'why-storytelling-is-the-future-of-marketing',
  '<p>People don''t buy products; they buy stories. In a saturated digital world, emotional connection is the strongest currency a brand can have.</p><h2>The Science of Story</h2><p>Stories activate parts of the brain associated with empathy and sensory experiences. When a brand tells a story, it invites the audience to be part of a narrative, rather than just a passive consumer.</p><blockquote>"Marketing is no longer about the stuff that you make, but about the stories you tell." – Seth Godin</blockquote><p>From your "About Us" page to your social media captions, every touchpoint is an opportunity to weave your narrative. Authenticity is key—consumers can spot a fabricated story from a mile away.</p>',
  'People don''t buy products; they buy stories. Explore why emotional connection is the strongest currency a brand can have in a saturated digital world.',
